course: dictionary
lesson: 12262
title: Words that mean at the same time
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Contemporaneously is a formal word. It means at the same time as something else, or during the same period. It is an adverb, so it tells you how or when two things happen.
explain: «The alarm sounded, and contemporaneously the lights went out.» The alarm and the lights happen together, so contemporaneously means at the same time. Check by swapping in «at the same time»: the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Historians and lawyers use this word a lot. A note written contemporaneously is written at the time of the events, so it is more reliable than one written years later, when memories may have faded.
fact: Contemporaneously means at the same time as something else, or during the same period.
fact: Contemporaneously is an adverb: it tells how or when two things happen.
fact: In everyday English, people usually say «at the same time» instead.
fact: «Mia wrote her notes contemporaneously with the trip, so her details were accurate.»
fact: In history and law, a note written contemporaneously is written at the time of the events, so it is often better evidence.
exercise: «The alarm sounded, and contemporaneously the lights went out.» What does contemporaneously mean here? | Very loudly | Before anything else | *At the same time | Much later
exercise: A historian says a letter was written contemporaneously with the battle. What does this tell you? | It was never written at all | *It was written at the time of the battle | It was written a hundred years later | It was written about a different battle
exercise: Which words are closest in everyday English to contemporaneously? | a long time ago | *at the same time | far away | in the end
test: «Mia wrote her notes contemporaneously with the trip.» What does this mean? | Afterwards, a year later | Before the trip began | Only at night | *During the same time as the trip
test: Why is a note written contemporaneously more reliable than one written years later? | Because it is always in pencil | Because it is longer | Because a famous person wrote it | *Because it was written at the time, before memories fade
exam: Which sentence uses contemporaneously correctly? | The cat sat contemporaneously, but only in the box | Contemporaneously is a colour of paint | I will contemporaneously eat my lunch last week | *Two bands played contemporaneously on different stages
